### Create a transaction
POST http://localhost:8080/api/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "Groceries",
  "amount": 85.50,
  "category": "Food",
  "type": "EXPENSE"
}

### Get all transactions
GET http://localhost:8080/api/transactions


### Valid transaction
POST http://localhost:8080/api/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "Groceries",
  "amount": 85.50,
  "category": "Food",
  "type": "EXPENSE"
}

### Invalid transaction
POST http://localhost:8080/api/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "   ",
  "amount": -10,
  "category": "",
  "type": "INVALID"
}


### 1. Create a transaction
POST http://localhost:8080/api/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "Groceries",
  "amount": 85.50,
  "category": "Food",
  "type": "EXPENSE"
}

### 2. Get all transactions
GET http://localhost:8080/api/transactions

### 3. Get transaction with ID 1
GET http://localhost:8080/api/transactions/1

### 4. Update transaction with ID 1
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/transactions/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "Weekly groceries",
  "amount": 95.00,
  "category": "Food",
  "type": "EXPENSE"
}

### 5. Delete transaction with ID 1
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/transactions/1

### 6. Try to get the deleted transaction
GET http://localhost:8080/api/transactions/1

### Register a new user
POST http://localhost:8080/api/users/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "aksana@example.com",
  "password": "MySecurePassword123"
}
### Test: invalid email
POST http://localhost:8080/api/users/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "password": "MySecurePassword123"
}

### Test: password too short
POST http://localhost:8080/api/users/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "shortpassword@example.com",
  "password": "short"
}
